          "Around lines 968-977, `try { await _deleteFileIfPresent(file); try { await file.parent.delete(recursive: true); } catch (_) {} } catch (_) {}`.",
          "`_deleteFileIfPresent` (lines 979-982) already wraps its body in `try { ... } catch (_) {}`, so the outer try adds no recovery path.",
          "Cleanup failures are discarded silently at every level, so a real permission or disk fault during cover eviction produces no log."
