          "Doc comment on UpdateCheckException (lines 76-78): 'checkForUpdate returns null only when a verified release list has no newer version'.",
          "checkForUpdate lines 181-184: 'if (!_isAndroid) { return null; }' runs before any fetch or verification and returns null silently.",
          "Every other null return in checkForUpdate is guarded by _throwUnverified() when snapshot.verified is false (lines 195, 212, 233), so the early return is the sole exception."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either throw UpdateCheckException on the non-Android path, or narrow the doc comment to say that the Android-only guard returns null and that null from a verified list means no newer version. Choosing one keeps 'up to date' and 'could not check' distinguishable for callers.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "523f01cf"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Fixed in the refactor batch (dc17c94): see commit message; analyze and the full test suite pass (1869).",
